# mano-android-use agent rule

When controlling Android via this repo's MCP (`mano-android-use` / `mau`):

**Principle:** Host picks goal/plan; mau orchestrates; Grounder sees screenshots; L0 executes.

1. Start with `ready` (or `doctor` then `ready`). Honor `tips[]`, `screen.awake`, `text_backend.available`.
2. **Default multi-step path (Phase O-A):** Cursor → **several short `android_run`** (one SlotSpec stage each) — **not** one fat `android_run_plan` (CLI/`mau run-plan` OK for long plans). `package=` warm-ensure when known; `launch_app` / `cold_start=true` only for true relaunch. Do **not** open installed apps by typing Chinese in a browser. MCP defaults are short (`max_steps≈10`, ~90s soft budget). **Every** successful return includes `task_patch` + ResumeSpec (`resume`/`continue_hint`): merge into Host TaskState (OR-merge `progress` incl. `completed_slots` / `world` / `policy`; replace `resume`/`screen_digest`); on resume fill `do.*` (`omit_package`, `cold_start=false`, keep/replace `tree_hints`/`success_check` per stage) and pass `progress_json` from TaskState; honor `dont[]` (**no HOME / force_stop / rewrite_goal / propose_action loop**). Prefer `tree_hints` or「quoted」labels when the target is a stable a11y string so mau can tree-shortcut before VLM. After stage success, Host may set `completed_slots` + `world.sku_keys` / `cart_count` and `policy.banned_hint_labels` / `banned_act_classes` (do **not** expect mau to auto-infer SKUs). Guard NO_OPs redo `open_spec`/`confirm_add` when `target_key` already in `world.sku_keys`; payment still SafetyGateway.
2b. **On MCP `-32001` / empty Host timeout (Phase O-B, hard):** do **not** treat as failure and rewrite the goal. A≠B: short-run default prevents most losses; this path **recovers** when `task_patch` never arrived. (1) Call MCP/CLI **`resume_from_run`** (optional `slots_path=docs/examples/slots/meituan-dual-drink.slots.json`) or `journal_tail` + newest `runs/<id>/`. (2) Read `draft_progress` / `warnings` / `needs_confirm` — `cart_count` only from「已添加N件」; **never** use `goal_reached_stop_count` as件数; dual-drink needs N=2 before C/D. Confirm heuristics, then `find` if unsure. (3) Short `android_run` from `mcp_hint` / `resume.do`: omit `package=`, `cold_start=false`, **replace** `tree_hints`, pass `progress_json`. (4) Never open a fresh cold plan/HOME as the next move. See playbook §「A vs B」+「Lost MCP response」.
3. **Goals:** never put payment/submit button copy in the goal (e.g. avoid「立即支付」); say stop-before-pay instead. Meituan-class → short staged goals (搜 / 露菜单 / 规格加购) via **N× `android_run`** — **not one giant goal** or one Cursor-fat plan. **Recipe gates:** A enter-store needs **选规格/请输入商品名**（或 cart chrome）— bare「点菜」≠ DONE; dual-drink C/D need **已添加2件**（+去结算 on D）; never treat fixture plans as success truth. Templates: [`meituan-dual-drink-cart.json`](docs/examples/plans/meituan-dual-drink-cart.json) + slots; recipe [`docs/recipes/meituan.md`](docs/recipes/meituan.md).
4. **Host anti-redo / spin (hard):** one stage per slot; **replace `tree_hints` every stage** (SKU-first, never inherit bare「选规格」). **Never put success-only labels in `tree_hints`**. After STUCK/`TIME_BUDGET` → **`find` or `slot_peek`** → replace hints if wrong page → short `android_run` (do **not** reopen the same dull-hint add run; **do not** recover with L0 tap/BACK chains — Phase Q/R). On tool return `code=L0_BLOCKED_AFTER_STUCK`: follow `next` / `do` (find → short `android_run`); use `force_l0=true` only for one explicit correction (quota after STUCK is 1). Dual-drink before C: `find` a visible second drink then **one** C run — never hardcode store SKU into slots. After add looks done → `find` verify. Keep short MCP budgets; **do not** lengthen one run. Cost metric: **wall clock**, not tokens. **Enter-store once (R5):** success needs「选规格/请输入商品名」(or real menu); residual「去结算」/cart_count alone ≠ A DONE. **Compress gaps (R6):** read `continue_hint` immediately; find only when page/SKU changes.
5. Do **not** drive multi-step goals with `propose_action` chains or `propose_action(execute=true)` (deprecated). Use L0 `tap`/`swipe`/`type_text`/`press_button` only for install dialogs, one-off correction, or debug (e.g.「加入购物车」miss → tap clickable ancestor) — **never** as the STUCK recovery main path. mau **rejects** further Host L0 after STUCK once quota is used (`L0_BLOCKED_AFTER_STUCK`) unless `force_l0=true`. Unchanged screens are handled inside `android_run` (skip VLM → recover → STUCK); after `type`/`click`/`swipe`, a short act grace skips BACK.
6. Chinese `type_text` only if AdbKeyboard is available; otherwise tap/launch only and tell the user to install OpenATX AdbKeyboard.
7. APK install / ColorOS「继续安装」dialogs: handle with `observe`+`tap` or ask the human — not as an `android_run` goal.
8. If the screen is off, wake/unlock first; `android_run` only tries one `KEYCODE_WAKEUP`.
9. On `NEED_HUMAN` / `BLOCKED_BY_POLICY` for payment UI, stop.
10. Wireless ADB: if connect fails, re-pair/connect and refresh `MANO_DEVICE_SERIAL` (ports change). Prefer MCP L0 over shell `adb input tap` so safety + journal apply.
11. After every `android_run` / `android_run_plan`, **tell the user the cost**: quote `cost_report.narrative` (or summarize totals). Explain who spent time — `observe` (ADB tree/screenshot), `grounder` (VLM, also all tokens), `act` (tap/type/swipe). For plans, also list each stage’s `total_ms` / tokens / `dominant_phase`. When resuming, also surface `progress` / `resume.do` briefly so the user sees why the next short run is safe (no cold start).

